Package: BayesianTrial
Title: Bayesian Decision-Making for Clinical Trials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Jiangyan", family = "Zhao", email = "zhaojy2017@126.com", role = c("cre", "aut")),
    person(given = "Rongji", family = "Mu", email = "rjmu@sjtu.edu.cn", role = "aut")
  )
Maintainer: Jiangyan Zhao <zhaojy2017@126.com>
Description: Provides tools for evaluating Bayesian decision rules in
 clinical trials. For two-stage single-arm trials with binary
 endpoints, computes posterior probabilities under Beta-binomial
 models, estimates predictive probabilities of meeting prespecified
 final success criteria, and evaluates type I error rates, statistical
 power, and early stopping probabilities through Monte Carlo
 simulation. For methodological background on Bayesian phase II
 monitoring and predictive probabilities, see Thall and Simon (1994)
 <doi:10.2307/2533377> and Lee and Liu (2008)
 <doi:10.1177/1740774508089279>.
